---
# Blocking static analysis (CI runs `make tidy`). High-value bugprone /
# analyzer / performance checks stay on. Disabled checks are documented
# below — each fires on idiomatic systems code in this repo:
#   signed-bitwise ......... epoll/poll flag arithmetic (EPOLLIN|EPOLLOUT);
#                            the kernel APIs themselves use int flags.
#   easily-swappable ....... epoll_ctl/epoll_wait mirror POSIX signatures
#                            that cannot change; log_set(key, value) is the
#                            conventional order.
#   implicit-bool .......... poll revents bit-tests (revents & POLLIN).
#   trailing-comma ......... pure style.
#   cognitive-complexity ... single dispatch loops (Server/Admin start()).
#   member-function-const .. const-churn on epoll handlers, no safety value.
#   magic-numbers .......... protocol constants; identifier-length: short
#                            fd/ev names are conventional.
Checks: 'bugprone-*,clang-analyzer-*,performance-*,readability-*,-readability-magic-numbers,-readability-identifier-length,-bugprone-signed-bitwise,-bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,-readability-implicit-bool-conversion,-readability-trailing-comma,-readability-function-cognitive-complexity,-readability-make-member-function-const,-readability-convert-member-functions-to-static'
WarningsAsErrors: true
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/.*'
CheckOptions:
  - key: readability-braces-around-statements.ShortStatementLines
    value: 1
...
